    "name": "Hyundai",
    "description": "Founded in 1967, Hyundai Motor Company now presents itself as a mobility company as well as an automaker, with its official history tracing the shift from the Ulsan assembly plant to current IONIQ electric vehicles.",
    "rawDescription": "Founded in 1967, Hyundai Motor Company now presents itself as a mobility company as well as an automaker, with its official history tracing the shift from the Ulsan assembly plant to current IONIQ electric vehicles. On the captured Korean product surfaces, that broad automotive identity resolves into a restrained interface: black and white text, a deep navy action color (`#002c5f`), and loaded HyundaiSans families. The documented vehicle-design direction, Sensuous Sportiness, has been Hyundai's design philosophy since 2018; it connects emotional appeal with structure, proportion, styling, and technology. This reference keeps that official vehicle-design context separate from web claims: it describes the captured KR product UI, not a universal Hyundai design system.\n\nThe product capture favors flat, rectangular actions for its repeated navy vehicle CTA, but it is not a zero-radius system: the selected carousel control has a 6px radius and the chatbot is circular. Deep navy (`#002c5f`) is the repeated product action color; teal (`#007fa8`) appears in captured carousel controls, while cyan (`#00aad2`) appears on the chatbot. Black (`#000000`), white (`#ffffff`), muted gray (`#999999`), utility gray (`#444444`), and the dark footer (`#1c1b1b`) are also directly observed.",
